.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.TH TUIIRSS 1 "September 2026" "tuituirss 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tuituirss \- terminal client for Tiny Tiny RSS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuituirss
.RB [ \-c | \-\-config
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-theme
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-dark | \-\-light | \-\-mono ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuituirss
is a fast, keyboard-driven terminal client for the self-hosted
.B Tiny Tiny RSS
reader. It talks to an existing tt\-rss server exclusively through the official
JSON API, so no server\-side changes are required beyond enabling API access for
your user.
.PP
The interface has three panes: a sidebar of virtual feeds, labels and
categories; a headline list; and an article reader. All network calls are
synchronous and a one\-line status bar reports progress and errors.
.PP
The password is never stored. It is read from the
.B TTUIRSS_PASSWORD
environment variable when set, and otherwise prompted for on startup.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIpath\fR
Read configuration from
.IR path
instead of the default
.IR ~/.tuituirssrc.json .
.TP
.BR \-\-theme " " \fIname\fR
Use the named color theme. Valid names are
.BR dark " (the default), " light ", and " mono .
The
.B mono
theme emits no ANSI color sequences at all and distinguishes state with
terminal attributes (reverse, bold, dim, underline) only.
.TP
.B \-\-dark
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-theme dark" .
.TP
.B \-\-light
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-theme light" .
.TP
.B \-\-mono
Shorthand for
.BR "\-\-theme mono" .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is a JSON object, by default read from
.IR ~/.tuituirssrc.json .
The following fields are recognized:
.TP
.B server_url
Full URL of the tt\-rss
.B api/
endpoint (required).
.TP
.B username
tt\-rss login name (required).
.TP
.B data_dir
Directory for the session cache and logs. Defaults to
.IR ~/.tuituirss .
.TP
.B insecure
Boolean. When true, TLS certificate verification is skipped. Only use this
for self\-signed certificates on trusted networks.
.TP
.B ca_file
Optional path to a custom CA bundle.
.TP
.B browser
Command used to open article links. The value is split on whitespace and
executed directly (without a shell), with the URL appended as the final
argument, so arguments such as
.B firefox \-\-new\-tab
are allowed. Defaults to
.BR $BROWSER ,
then
.B xdg\-open
on Linux or
.B open
on macOS.
.TP
.B theme
Color theme name:
.BR dark " (default), " light ", or " mono .
.TP
.B timeout_sec
Network timeout in seconds. Defaults to 30.
.TP
.B debug
Boolean. When true, write a debug log (credentials are redacted).
.TP
.B log_file
Log path. Defaults to
.IR data_dir/tuituirss.log
when
.B debug
is enabled.
.SH KEY BINDINGS
The full list is shown in\-app with
.BR ? .
The main bindings are:
.TP
.BR j ", " k " / " Up ", " Down
Move the selection down / up in a list.
.TP
.BR g ", " G " / " Home ", " End
Jump to the first / last item.
.TP
.BR h ", " l " / " Tab " / " Shift\-Tab
Move focus between panes.
.TP
.B Enter
Open the selected feed, category, or article.
.TP
.B Space
Load the selected headline into the article pane without changing focus.
.TP
.BR Up " / " Right ", " Down " / " Left
In the article pane, select the next / previous link detected in the post.
.TP
.B Enter
In the article pane, open the selected link in the external browser.
.TP
.BR j " / " k " / " PgDn " / " PgUp
In the article pane, scroll the article.
.TP
.BR r ", " s ", " p
Toggle read/unread, starred, or published.
.TP
.B n
Jump to the next unread headline.
.TP
.B x
Mark the current view (or the selected feed/category) as read.
.TP
.B m
Set a note (an empty value clears it).
.TP
.BR + " / " \-
Increase / decrease the score.
.TP
.B L
Open the label picker.
.TP
.B a
Cycle the view mode.
.TP
.B /
Filter headlines.
.TP
.BR A ", " D ", " u
Subscribe, unsubscribe, or force an update of a feed.
.TP
.B o
Toggle the split / article\-only layout.
.TP
.B R
Refresh the sidebar and current headlines.
.TP
.BR q " / " Esc
Go back one level; quit from the sidebar.
.TP
.B ?
Show the help overlay.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TTUIRSS_PASSWORD
Password used for login, skipping the interactive prompt. Useful for scripting.
.TP
.B BROWSER
Default external browser command, used when the
.B browser
configuration field is unset.
.TP
.B HOME
Used to locate the default configuration and data directories.
.TP
.B TERM
The terminal type, as usual for curses applications.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.tuituirssrc.json
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I ~/.tuituirss/
Default data directory (mode 0700).
.TP
.I ~/.tuituirss/session\-<sha1>.json
Cached session, keyed by a hash of the server URL (mode 0600).
.TP
.I ~/.tuituirss/tuituirss.log
Debug log when
.B debug
is enabled.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Configuration, initialization, or login failure.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid command\-line usage.
.SH SECURITY
Feed and article strings are untrusted. Displayed text is sanitized: control
characters, bidi overrides and zero\-width marks are removed, invalid UTF\-8 is
dropped, and article HTML is converted to plain text before display.
.PP
URLs are only passed to the configured browser as an
.BR execvp (3)
argument (no shell is involved) and only after the user explicitly selects one,
so feed content cannot inject shell commands or terminal escapes.
.PP
TLS verification is on by default and redirects are not followed. The password
is never written to disk; session files are created mode 0600.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR curl (1),
.BR ncurses (3)
.PP
The project's
.I README.md
and
.I PLAN.md
describe the design and configuration in more detail.
.SH LICENSE
MIT. tuituirss is an independent client that speaks the tt\-rss JSON API and
contains no tt\-rss code.
